# FoulFox OS package set.
# Installed into the live image's chroot. Grouped by purpose.

# ── Kernel + firmware (broad plug-and-play hardware support) ──────────────────
linux-image-amd64
firmware-linux
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-misc-nonfree
# Broadcom/Cypress wifi + Bluetooth firmware (brcmfmac / many laptop BT radios).
# Intel/Realtek/Atheros BT firmware already ships in the bundles above.
firmware-brcm80211
# MediaTek WiFi (MT7921/MT7922/MT7925) — covered by firmware-misc-nonfree
# in Debian bookworm (firmware-mediatek was merged; no separate package exists).
# Broadcom NetXtreme I/II Ethernet — common in workstations and older desktops.
firmware-bnx2
firmware-bnx2x
# Qualcomm/Atheros Ethernet (QCA8xxx NICs on many consumer motherboards).
# Covered by firmware-misc-nonfree but listed explicitly for clarity.

# ── Networking (auto bring-up, wired + wireless) ─────────────────────────────
network-manager
network-manager-gnome
iproute2
iw
wireless-tools
# WPA2/WPA3 supplicant — required for joining protected WiFi networks.
# NetworkManager pulls this as a dependency but listing it explicitly ensures
# it is always present even if NM dependency resolution changes.
wpasupplicant
# DNS resolution: systemd-resolved provides a local stub DNS resolver that NM
# writes to automatically. Without it, NM falls back to writing /etc/resolv.conf
# directly, which can race with live-config on boot and leave the system
# temporarily with no nameserver. resolved also handles mDNS and LLMNR.
systemd-resolved

# ── Bluetooth (plug-and-play pairing/management) ─────────────────────────────
# bluez provides bluetoothd + the bluetoothctl CLI the api-server drives. The
# BT controller firmware rides in the firmware-* bundles above (incl. brcm80211).
bluez

# ── Storage / removable media (USB frontload + NTFS/exFAT/FAT drives) ────────
udisks2
ntfs-3g
exfatprogs
dosfstools
# parted (+ its partprobe) is what foulfox-storage-setup drives to add the
# optional 'foulfox-persist' partition in trailing free space. Without it the
# Storage Setup auto-partition path dead-ends with TABLE_UNREADABLE on-device.
# (partx/findmnt/flock come from util-linux and mkfs.ext4 from e2fsprogs, both
# Priority: required, so they are always present in the base.)
parted
# gdisk provides sgdisk — GPT manipulation used by foulfox-install-to-disk to
# create the EFI + root partition table when installing to an internal disk.
gdisk
rsync

# ── Virtualization stack (Windows guest) ─────────────────────────────────────
qemu-system-x86
qemu-utils
ovmf
# ISO authoring for auto-provisioning: cloud-init seed (Linux) + autounattend
# answer-file CD (Windows). Without it both auto-download paths fail at the
# seed/answer-ISO step on the flashed appliance.
xorriso
swtpm
virt-viewer
spice-client-gtk
usbutils
pciutils

# ── NVIDIA GPU driver (local AI acceleration) ────────────────────────────────
# Proprietary driver for GeForce cards (GTX 1660 = Turing, supported by
# bookworm's 535 series). nvidia-driver pulls nvidia-kernel-dkms, which builds
# the module against the live kernel at image-build time (headers below).
# Without a bound GPU the baked Ollama falls back to CPU — slower but works.
nvidia-driver
firmware-misc-nonfree
linux-headers-amd64

# ── Graphical kiosk session ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
xserver-xorg
# Last-resort X drivers so a failed GPU driver can never mean "no screen":
# nouveau (NVIDIA open driver, used by foulfox-gpu-fallback when the
# proprietary module won't load) + dumb framebuffer/vesa fallbacks.
xserver-xorg-video-nouveau
xserver-xorg-video-fbdev
xserver-xorg-video-vesa
xinit
x11-xserver-utils
openbox
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter
chromium
# General-purpose browser alongside the Chromium kiosk: openable as a normal
# window over the kiosk via foulfox-open-browser (shell button / W-f shortcut).
firefox-esr

# ── UEFI + Secure Boot boot support ─────────────────────────────────────────
# grub-efi-amd64: GRUB EFI binary — gives the iso-hybrid an EFI System
# Partition so modern UEFI laptops (HP, Dell, Lenovo, …) recognise the USB as
# bootable without needing Legacy/CSM mode or disabling Secure Boot.
# grub-efi-amd64-signed + shim-signed: the Microsoft-trusted shim chain that
# lets the image boot on machines with Secure Boot ON (the default on most
# consumer laptops shipped with Windows).
grub-efi-amd64
grub-efi-amd64-signed
shim-signed

# ── Live system (live-build boot + config) ───────────────────────────────────
# By default live-build installs these in a SEPARATE, later apt transaction
# ("lb_chroot_live-packages"). That incremental install re-resolves the live
# packages against the already-installed desktop stack and dead-ends with:
#   "libgtk-3-common : Depends: dconf-gsettings-backend ... not going to be installed"
#   "E: ... pkgProblemResolver::Resolve generated breaks"
# i.e. apt cannot add the live packages on top of the GUI without proposing to
# drop the gsettings backend, so it gives up (exit 100). Listing them here
# installs them in the SAME combined transaction as the GUI stack -- which
# resolves cleanly, exactly like Debian's own desktop live images -- so the later
# live-packages pass finds them already present and becomes a no-op.
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd

# ── Runtimes for the FoulFox services ────────────────────────────────────────
# Node.js 20 is installed via the 0005-nodejs20.hook.chroot (NodeSource repo)
# because Debian bookworm's 'nodejs' package is v18 and FoulFox apps need >=20.
python3
python3-venv
python3-pip
build-essential
# The app installer extracts uploaded/bundled FoulFox App zips with unzip;
# without it every zip install (incl. the bundled default apps) fails.
unzip
# zstd: the Ollama runtime tarball (0040 hook) is a .tar.zst since Ollama
# v0.32 — without zstd the bake step cannot extract it.
zstd

# ── Taskbar ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tint2: the bottom-of-screen taskbar (one button per open window + clock) so
# background windows always have a visible dock; config in /etc/xdg/tint2.
tint2

# ── Window tray ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# wmctrl: lets the api-server list open X windows and re-activate a minimized
# one (the shell's taskbar/tray). Without it the tray simply reports
# unavailable — but a minimized Discord/Firefox would be unreachable.
wmctrl

# ── Screenshots ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# scrot: lightweight X11 screenshotter used by foulfox-screenshot (PrintScreen
# key binding). libnotify-bin: the notify-send binary that shows the "Screenshot
# saved" toast after capture.
scrot
libnotify-bin

# ── Convenience ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
sudo
ca-certificates
curl
less
nano
